Bees/ants are best fight in corridors, when only one (or two) can attack
you each turn. Fighting bees in an open room is suicide (especially for
early PC, when ascencion-ready, a swarm of bees should not be harmful).
Learn when to run (backward) or not run (forward) and let the ennemies
come to you (if they spend their move coming, you'll be first to attack).
Choose your fight and, more important, choose the your position. Retreat
until you're in a position where you can fight at your advantage. Usually
a turn in a corridor where both you and your pet can attack the same
monster while only one monster can attack you. Don't be afraid to hide
behind your pet and let it do the job.

